ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.fairfaxva.gov/files/assets/city/v/2/
 historic-resources/images/civil-war-exhibit-signage-24-x-36-in.jpg?dimensi
 on=smallthumbnail&w=150&h=100
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:From 1861 to 1865\, Americans fought each other with a ferocit
 y unseen in the country’s history. The immediate cause of the war was th
 e secession of the Southern states. However\, the roots lay in growing ten
 sions over slavery. By the time the last shots were fired\, as many as 750
 \,000 Americans had been killed\, and four million enslaved people were fr
 eed.\n\nDetails: https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Events-directory/Historic-Resou
 rces/Q3-JulAugSep-HH/The-Civil-War
LOCATION:Fairfax Museum and Visitor Center\, 10209 Main St.\,  22030
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Events-directory/Historic-Resources/Q3-JulAu
 gSep-HH/The-Civil-War
END:VEVENT
